Lipopeptide (脂肽类) antibiotics
❖ Daptomycin 达托霉素:
考
❑ The first FDA approved lipopeptide antibiotics;
❑ For G+ bacteria;
❑ Dependent on Ca2+ and phosphatidylglycerol (PG);
❑ Pore-forming, lipid extraction, and blocking cell wall synthesis;
❑ High side-effects, low resistance.
(adapted) Cold Spring Harb. Perspect. Med., 2016, 6(11)

Lipopeptide (脂肽类) antibiotics
❖ Polymyxin 多粘菌素:
考
❑ For G- bacteria;
❑ Binds to lipopolysaccharide (LPS);
❑ Disruption to both OM and CM;
❑ High side-effects (neurotoxic and nephrotoxic), low resistance.
J. Antibiot. (Tokyo), 2022, 75(11)

Decreased antibiotics influx
❖ By reduction of uptake:
❑ Reduce influx channels (porins);
❑ Reduce outer membrane permeability (LPS);
❑ Increase cell wall;
❑ Biofilms formation.
Decrease permeability Low metabolic activity
Protect persister cells Allowing AMR gene transfer
