Rational use of antiviral drugs
❖ Antiviral agents used in combination:
❑ Drugs used in combination should target different viral gene products;
❑ Splitting a treatment into two steps: induction and maintenance, drugs
administered in the two steps should be different;
❑ Targeting of cellular functions needed for the virus life cycle;
❑ Combined use of immunotherapy and chemotherapy;
❑ Lethal mutagenesis or virus extinction by excess of mutations
introduced during viral replication.
